{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\eng\\090.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Use of Language", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[189, 137], [475, 142], [475, 182], [189, 178]]}, {"text": "Simple Sentences", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[127, 221], [382, 215], [383, 248], [128, 254]]}, {"text": "A sentence is commonly defined as \"a complete unit of thought.\"", "conf": 0.955, "box": [[121, 265], [894, 268], [894, 308], [121, 305]]}, {"text": "A simple sentence is the simplest form of a sentence that has", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[122, 310], [846, 310], [846, 345], [122, 345]]}, {"text": "only one independent main clause. It conveys a complete", "conf": 0.941, "box": [[122, 351], [802, 351], [802, 387], [122, 387]]}, {"text": "Points to know!", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[960, 359], [1136, 361], [1135, 385], [960, 383]]}, {"text": "The predicate tells us about", "conf": 0.879, "box": [[905, 385], [1190, 391], [1189, 418], [904, 412]]}, {"text": "meaning.", "conf": 0.79, "box": [[121, 396], [234, 396], [234, 427], [121, 427]]}, {"text": "the subject. It always", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[903, 417], [1119, 421], [1118, 448], [902, 444]]}, {"text": "includesthemain verb.", "conf": 0.851, "box": [[901, 449], [1143, 452], [1142, 476], [901, 473]]}, {"text": "Thebasicparts of a sentence are the subject and the verb", "conf": 0.893, "box": [[121, 477], [805, 477], [805, 506], [121, 506]]}, {"text": "The subject is usually a noun-a word (or phrase) that names a", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[118, 517], [865, 519], [865, 549], [118, 546]]}, {"text": "person, place, or thing.", "conf": 0.933, "box": [[117, 560], [392, 555], [393, 588], [118, 592]]}, {"text": "Theverb (orpredicate)usuallyfollowsthesubjectandidentifies", "conf": 0.943, "box": [[119, 600], [874, 600], [874, 629], [119, 629]]}, {"text": "an action orastateof being.", "conf": 0.863, "box": [[115, 637], [456, 640], [456, 673], [115, 670]]}, {"text": "Example", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[353, 692], [458, 692], [458, 727], [353, 727]]}, {"text": "TheOlympi